"When you stop, your heartbeat and breathing do not drop at once. For a few minutes your body keeps working to pay back the oxygen it borrowed and to cool down. The better your fitness, the faster you recover. And fitness can be trained. If you are active often, your heart muscle grows stronger and pushes out more blood with every beat, so it does not have to beat as often. Some top long-distance athletes have a resting heart rate below 50.": "40d65cc9cdb5",
